---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: VOCA-UK
favicon: /assets/img/vocauk/favicon.ico
ogImage: /assets/img/vocauk/og.jpg
ogImageWidth: 1500
ogImageHeight: 594
ogImageAlt: VOCA-UK logo above Kagamine Len, Kagamine Rin, Hatsune Miku, Megurine Luka and IA
themeColor: '#1ebab0'
description: Before VOCAWAVES there was VOCA-UK, a fan VOCALOID concert project based in the UK, active from 2022 to 2023.
---
{% from "macros.njk" import setlist %}
<div class="vocauk">
    <header class="hero" id="top">
        <video class="uk-hero-video" playsinline autoplay muted loop poster="/assets/img/vocauk/hero-poster.webp" aria-hidden="true">
            <source src="/assets/img/vocauk/hero.mp4" type="video/mp4">
        </video>

        <div class="hero-text wrap">
            <img class="uk-logo" src="/assets/img/vocauk/logo.webp" width="1000" height="206" alt="VOCA-UK Logo">
            <h1><b>Fan</b> VOCALOID concert</h1>
            <p class="hero-years">2022 - 2023</p>
            <p class="hero-thanks">Thank you for being a part of our journey!</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section class="history" aria-labelledby="history-title">
            <div class="wrap uk-center">
                <h2 id="history-title"><b>Our</b> story</h2>
                <p class="intro">VOCA-UK began as a goal to bring VOCALOID culture to Northern England, as the official
                    events and organisations were all based in London.</p>

                <ol class="timeline">
                    {%- for item in vocauk.timeline %}
                    {%- if item.type == "milestone" %}
                    <li class="milestone{% if item.key %} milestone-key{% endif %}">
                        <time datetime="{{ item.date }}">{{ item.dateLabel }}</time>
                        <div>
                            <p>{{ item.text }}</p>
                            {%- if item.link.external %}
                            <p class="uk-milestone-link"><a href="{{ item.link.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="external">{{ item.link.label }}<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
                            {%- elif item.link %}
                            <p class="uk-milestone-link"><a href="{{ item.link.url }}">{{ item.link.label }}</a></p>
                            {%- endif %}
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    {%- else %}
                    <li class="show">
                        <time datetime="{{ item.date }}">{{ item.dateLabel }}</time>
                        <div class="show-body">
                            <h3>{{ item.title }}</h3>
                            <p class="show-place">{{ item.place }}</p>
                            <p>{{ item.text }}</p>
                            {%- if item.link %}
                            <p><a href="{{ item.link.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="external">{{ item.link.label }}<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
                            {%- endif %}
                            {{ setlist(item.setlist, item.setlistUnordered) }}
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    {%- endif %}
                    {%- endfor %}
                </ol>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
            <div class="work-title">
                <div class="wrap uk-center">
                <h2 id="work-title"><b>What</b> was VOCA-UK?</h2>
                <p class="intro">A not-for-profit, unofficial 3D CGI concert project featuring virtual singers from
                    Japan. The name combined "VOCALOID" and "UK", and our logo recoloured the Union Jack with the
                    Kagamine, Miku and MEIKO colours.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="band band-teal">
                <div class="wrap band-grid uk-left">
                    <div>
                        <h3><b>In-person</b> concerts</h3>
                        <p>One of the first vocalsynth projection-based systems in the UK, we brought the virtual singers to life on stages across the country.</p>
                        <p>Every concert had its own set list. We also had smaller live events called "MINI".</p>
                    </div>
                    <img class="uk-band-photo" src="/assets/img/vocauk/rakucon.webp" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy"
                        alt="Capture showing the audience, Rin and Una at RakuCon 2022">
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="band band-red">
                <div class="wrap band-grid band-grid-flip uk-right">
                    <div>
                        <h3><b>Online</b> concerts</h3>
                        <p>YouTube-based experiences with music videos, stories and unique elements. A mixture of different formats and styles.</p>
                        <p>We used these to experiment with new ideas, and to reach audiences who couldn't attend in person.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="band-photos">
                        <img src="/assets/img/vocauk/temple.webp" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy"
                            alt="Senbonzakura Miku">
                        <img src="/assets/img/vocauk/phone.webp" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy"
                            alt="Our experiment with vertical video and AR">
                        <img src="/assets/img/vocauk/luka.webp" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy"
                            alt="Megurine Luka from the online show">
                        <img src="/assets/img/vocauk/red.webp" width="1200" height="490" loading="lazy"
                            alt="GUMI from the online show">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="band band-blue">
                <div class="wrap uk-left">
                    <h3><b>The</b> singers</h3>
                    <ul class="uk-singers">
                        {%- for singer in vocauk.singers %}
                        <li>
                            <img src="/assets/img/vocauk/singers/{{ singer.image }}.webp" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" alt="">
                            <span class="uk-singer-name"><b>{{ singer.first }}</b>{% if singer.second %} {{ singer.second }}{% endif %}</span>
                            <span class="uk-singer-owner">{{ singer.owner }}</span>
                        </li>
                        {%- endfor %}
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="band uk-next">
                <div class="wrap">
                    <h3><b>What</b> came next</h3>
                    <p>In January 2024 the project restarted under a new name, VOCAWAVES, to better reflect our mission
                        and values.</p>
                    <a class="home-link" href="/">Read the VOCAWAVES story</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
        <div class="wrap">
            <img class="footer-logo" src="/assets/img/vocauk/logo.webp" width="1000" height="206" loading="lazy"
                alt="VOCA-UK">
            <ul class="socials">
                <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@vocauk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube</a></li>
                <li><a href="/">VOCAWAVES</a></li>
            </ul>

            <p class="legal">VOCA-UK was a non-commercial fan-run project, and no income was generated. The project was
                not affiliated with any of the companies or individuals who licensed the characters, models, motions and
                music to the public.</p>
            <p class="legal">"VOCALOID" and "VOCALO" are registered trademarks of Yamaha Corporation. This page depicts
                the characters Hatsune Miku, Kagamine Rin, Kagamine Len, Megurine Luka, MEIKO and KAITO of Crypton Future
                Media, INC. based on the
                <a href="https://piapro.jp/license/pcl/summary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">piapro Character License</a>.</p>
            <p class="legal">Video contains stage by Philippe-n-12 and motion by ゲッツ/すぱにぃ/ノン (using LipFaceMaker).
                Concert images contain models by YYB, ITzTETO, Roki-P, Maydayfireball and kuuwanko&amp;Rennya; motions by
                Touzoku Tsubaki, mobiusP, KAZUSA, 菖蒲（あやめ）＠剣舞Ｐ, SWA 104 and Anatroccolo (using LipFaceMaker); and some
                stages by komena, Jin and Mumumu. Performer models by YYB, Maydayfireball, kuuwanko&amp;Rennya, Jjinomu,
                Rubeeish, FreezyChan-3Dreams and ITzTETO. Some poses by PandaSwagg2002.</p>
            <p class="legal">&copy; 2022-2023 VOCA-UK TEAM. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <a class="to-top" href="#top" aria-label="Back to top"></a>
    <script src="/assets/js/index.js"></script>
</div>
